# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values to activate the contact form.
#
# All three come from your EmailJS dashboard (https://dashboard.emailjs.com):
#   Service ID   -> Email Services  -> the service you send through
#   Template ID  -> Email Templates -> the template the form fills in
#   Public key   -> Account -> General -> "Public Key"
#
# The public key is meant to be shipped in the client bundle — it is not a secret.
# Lock delivery down with EmailJS's allowed-origins and rate-limit settings instead.
#
# The template must use these variables: {{userName}}, {{userEmail}}, {{message}}.
#
# Leave any of these unset and the form still validates, but tells the visitor it is
# not connected yet instead of failing silently.
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
